it's been 21 years since diablo ii and  if you missed the seminal classic or are  hankering to revisit then the remaster  diablo 2 resurrected is upon us and is  coming to consoles for the first time  the classic game's got a brand new look  as well as a few tweaks and additions to  modernize the experience for a new and  returning audience so here's everything  you need to know and all the biggest  changes for more diablo and to keep up  on what's happening at activision  blizzard with regard to the ongoing  legal action taken by the california  department of fair employment and  housing make sure to subscribe  diablo 2 resurrected is the complete  edition of the original game including  the base game and its lord of  destruction expansion the most  significant change is the new visual  style which presents the game at 4k  resolution while the original was 2d the  remaster runs on a new 3d engine that  has reimagined many iconic characters  locations loot and monsters it paints  over the 2d sprites with 3d rendered  models to give it new life the original  game's cinematics and soundtrack have  also been rebuilt from the ground up but  if you still want to experience the  original diablo 2 as it was you can tap  the legacy button and instantly swap to  the classic look in real time now  playable in modern monitor resolutions  and speaking of monitors while you'll be  able to play the game on an ultra wide  it won't support the full 21.9 ultra  wide aspect ratio instead only extending  to 19.9 21 9 support was included in the  game's technical alpha but was removed  because it broke the game specifically  playing at an ultra-wide aspect ratio  made it so that players could attack  from further ranges than the game was  designed for enemies targeted from the  extended range ultrawide monitors  provide simply failed to recognize they  were being attacked and as a result  didn't react on a mechanical level  resurrected doesn't change much of the  core gameplay from the original game  which was the intent according to  blizzard however there are updates to  the game that aim to make the dungeon  crawling and power growth less tedious  for your chosen class like auto gold  pickup more helpful tutorial tips and  reminders to use your skill points you  can toggle these on and off at will the  biggest change that relates to the flow  and management of loot is the new shared  stash box allowing you to easily share  items with your different characters in  the original game if you wanted to share  items amongst all your characters you  would have to find an empty server drop  your gear swap over to a different  character and pick up the items with  them to do so this new mechanic doesn't  substantially change the game but it  does make things a bit more manageable  for dedicated players with regard to  ladders blizzard revealed that in order  to ensure server stability at launch the  game's first ladder season will come  shortly after the game's release but  won't be available on day one and that  formerly ladder exclusive unique items  rune words and recipes will be included  in non-ladder multiplayer and single  player for the first time ladder seasons  usually last around 6 months and require  new characters to be created  and there are ladders for both normal  and hardcore aka permadeath characters  but of course one of the biggest changes  is that the game is available on  consoles for the first time in regards  to how resurrected handles displaying  and mapping abilities blizzard took cues  from its console port of diablo 3  showing certain abilities in a tray on  the lower part of the hud the game also  controls differently on console you have  direct control of your character's  movement with your thumbstick whereas on  pc you click on a destination and your  character will wander over looting is  also different compared to the pc  version instead of holding down a button  to see loot on the ground and then  clicking to pick it up the console  version automatically displays items on  the ground for players nearby simply  walk over items slowly to pick them up  diablo 2 resurrected will still have  online multiplayer along with bringing  back eight player games resurrected's  online infrastructure has been updated  to protect players against cheaters and  those looking to hack however it has  been confirmed that the remaster will  not have cross play amongst the  different platforms tcp ip multiplayer  which allowed players to connect via lan  or other peer-to-peer connections  instead of official servers will not be  present in the remaster and blizzard  cites security risks as the reason  you'll be limited to dedicated blizzard  servers when you play online it will  also allow for cross progression meaning  if you've been hanging onto your pc save  file for 20 years your local single  player save will work  back at blizzcon earlier this year  blizzard spoke about the different  lessons learned from the making of  warcraft 3 reforged which was released  to a mixed reception from fans much a  fan disappointment for warcraft 3 came  from blizzard using the remaster to  replace the original game on battle.net  making it the only way to play the last  strategy game in the warcraft series in  our talk with blizzard at the time the  studio stated that they plan to keep the  original version of diablo 2 on  battle.net which will be playable  alongside the remaster while resurrected  will keep the classic game and visuals  in its legacy mode players who are still  used to the original can opt to play  that instead  the remaster of diablo 2 is coming from  both blizzard entertainment and  developer vicarious visions the latter  previously worked on the crash bandicoot  insane trilogy remaster and 2020's tony  hawk pro skater 1 and 2. so the studio  has quite the pedigree when it comes to  updating classic games along with  handling the remaster vicarious visions  is also behind the process of bringing  diablo 2 to consoles which as i  mentioned earlier marks the game's first  appearance away from pc  diablo 2 resurrected is the first major  game release from blizzard as parent  company activision blizzard continues to  address allegations from a state of  california lawsuit that's accusing  parent company activision blizzard of  fostering a frat boy culture of  harassment and discrimination against  women thousands of employees signed an  open letter condemning how the company  responded to the lawsuit and staged a  massive walk out on july 28 2021 the  california department of fair employment  and housing later updated its lawsuit  accusing the company of destroying  evidence pertinent to the investigation  following those allegations numerous  veteran blizzard employees left the  company with president j alan brack  stepping down and jen o'neil and mikey  barra taking over parent company  activision blizzard is also facing a  separate lawsuit from employees which  alleges that the company is using  coercive actions to prevent  organizational efforts to improve  working conditions it's also facing a  third lawsuit this time from its  shareholders who allege that the company  failed to notify them about the  department of fair employment and  housing's two-year investigation the sec  has also launched an investigation over  the company's handling of employees  allegations of sexual misconduct and  workplace discrimination and has  subpoenaed activision blizzard and  multiple senior executives including ceo  bobby kotick  [Music]  there's a link in the description where  we're keeping a timeline of all events  to do with the activision blizzard legal  action so make sure to keep an eye on  gamespot to keep up to date  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

